WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.242
Coding Exercise 3 asks you to return patients who do not have any lab results.

00:00:05.242 --> 00:00:09.507
Start by preserving all patients with a LEFT JOIN to lab results.

00:00:09.507 --> 00:00:14.477
When a patient has no matching lab row, the lab-side columns become NULL.

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:19.062
Then choose a right-side key that cannot be NULL in a real matched record.

00:00:19.062 --> 00:00:23.797
The lab test ID is a good choice because it identifies the lab row.

00:00:23.797 --> 00:00:26.372
Keep only rows where that key is NULL.

00:00:26.372 --> 00:00:31.942
Read your logic as a sentence: keep all patients, try to match a lab result,

00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:35.822
and then keep only the patients for whom no lab row was found.

00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:37.997
This is the anti-join pattern.

00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:43.967
You can reuse the same reasoning to find customers with no orders, students with no submissions,

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:47.938
employees with no training record, or products with no sales.
